{"content":"Fixed the regression in boltons/urlutils.py's URL.get_authority() method. The bug was an inverted condition: `if not (self.password):` was used instead of `if self.password:` when deciding whether to add the ':password' part after the username in the authority string. This caused the password to be incorrectly omitted when present (or spuriously added when absent/empty), breaking roundtrip serialization, userinfo rendering, and quoted-userinfo rendering.

Verified manually: `URL('http://wiki:pa$$a@hatnote.com').to_text()` now correctly returns 'http://wiki:pa$$a@hatnote.com' (previously would have dropped the password), and `URL('http://wiki@hatnote.com').to_text()` correctly returns 'http://wiki@hatnote.com' with no password shown.

No local test suite was found in this checkout (only the boltons/ source and docs/ directories exist, no tests/ directory), so the fix was verified via direct interactive checks matching the reported failure scenario.","tool_calls":[]}
